# Prettier's scope in this repository is the two TypeScript trees,
# `frontend/` and `tests/e2e/`, and nothing else.
#
# The list below is an allowlist rather than a denylist: everything is
# excluded, then those two directories are added back. A denylist would
# silently pull in each new top-level directory, and Prettier claims more
# here than you would expect. Left unrestricted it reformats the Askama
# templates under `crates/noombat-api/templates/` (it reads them as plain
# HTML and does not know what `{% %}` is), the Compose files, and every
# Markdown file, where the prose uses semantic line breaks that Prettier
# reflows away.
#
# Patterns resolve relative to this file, so this only behaves as intended
# while it stays at the repository root.

/*
!/frontend
!/tests
/tests/*
!/tests/e2e

# Build output and dependencies.
/frontend/dist/
**/node_modules/

# Lockfiles are YAML, so Prettier would claim them. pnpm writes them in
# its own style and Dependabot regenerates them wholesale, so formatting
# them here would put every dependency pull request in permanent conflict
# with the format check.
**/pnpm-lock.yaml
